course: dictionary
lesson: 13988
title: Longbows and archers
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words come from history, and you can often work out their meaning from the words around them. «The archer pulled back the string of his longbow and let the arrow fly.» An archer is a person who shoots with a bow, so a longbow must be a kind of bow.
explain: «The longbowmen stood in a line and waited for the enemy.» Men who are called longbowmen use longbows, so the word names both a weapon and the soldier who uses it. Try your meaning in the sentence: a large bow for shooting arrows still makes sense.
explain: The clue «made from one piece of wood» tells you a longbow is simple and strong, not a machine. When context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A longbow is a large bow, about as tall as a man.
fact: A longbow is usually made from one piece of wood, often yew.
fact: In the Middle Ages, the longbow was the famous weapon of English and Welsh archers.
fact: English longbowmen helped the English win at Crécy in 1346 and at Agincourt in 1415.
fact: In stories about Robin Hood, he shoots a longbow.
exercise: «The archer pulled back the string of his longbow.» What is a longbow? | *A large bow for shooting arrows | A tall tower for watching the enemy | A small knife used for cutting wood | A wooden shield for soldiers
exercise: «The longbowman aimed carefully at the target.» What is a longbowman? | A farmer who grows yew trees | A cook who makes bread for an army | A rider who looks after horses | *An archer who shoots a longbow
exercise: A longbow was often made from which material? | Glass | *Yew wood | Plastic | Iron
test: At which battle in 1415 did English longbowmen help the English win? | Bannockburn | *Agincourt | Waterloo | Hastings
test: In the stories of Robin Hood, what weapon does he shoot? | A sword | A spear | *A longbow | A cannon
exam: What was the famous weapon of English and Welsh archers in the Middle Ages? | Catapult | Shield | *Longbow | Crossbow
